		(locked yes)
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "996b3503-fe1d-416d-a4c4-5655e7c1169d")
		(at 100 101.42 180)
		(descr "Amphenol F32Q-1A7H1-11024 (24-pos, 0.5mm, TOP contact). LOCAL REVERSE-PINOUT VARIANT of Connector_FFC-FPC:Amphenol_F32Q-1A7x1-11024 - signal pad NUMBERS reversed (N -> 25-N), ALL geometry/pads/silk/anchors UNCHANGED. Use because the display FPC folds 180deg to the PCB back: FPC pin1 = device-LEFT, so the netlist must reach the land that physically mates it. Schematic must wire conn pin N <-> FPC pin N straight 1:1 (this footprint does the reversal - do NOT also reverse in schematic). Silk pin-1 marker intentionally stays at the physical part's pin-1 corner. See FPC_CONNECTOR_PLACEMENT.md.")
